{
  "notes": [
    "Every vector is H_FIELDS_V1: preimage = u64_be(len(domain)) || domain || for each field u64_be(len(field)) || field; digest = SHA256(preimage).",
    "Field encoding (§1.2): string = strict UTF-8 bytes; bytes = raw bytes; uint32/uint64 = 4/8-byte big-endian; enum = uint32 big-endian.",
    "\"producer\" names the unexported keeper function the vector is executed against. The digest below is what that function returns when fed this vector's own inputs, not only what re-framing fields[] reproduces; a field swap inside the producer therefore fails here even when the swapped fields share an encoder.",
    "Regenerate with TRUEOPEN_REGEN_FIXTURES=1; the run rewrites the expectations and then fails on purpose so the consensus diff must be reviewed before it is committed.",
    "TRUEOPEN_UNBONDING_ID_V1 has no vector here on purpose. Its golden lives in x/hub/types/testdata/hub_domains_v1.json and stays the single copy; the executable binding to keeper.serviceUnbondingID reads that file rather than restating its seven fields, because two copies of one frozen preimage can disagree.",
    "Vectors for domains removed in Wire v0.3.0 were deleted from this file in the same revision that removed the domains, so it is no longer a byte copy of the upstream node fixture; source_path still records where the retained vectors came from."
  ],
